<title>USA: U.S. cash soymeal - Drop in futures prompts sales.</title>
<headline>U.S. cash soymeal - Drop in futures prompts sales.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soymeal sales continued this week at a moderate pace, with lower CBOT soymeal futures since last week attracting price-conscious buyers, dealers said.</p>
<p>CBOT July soymeal futures fell to a low Tuesday morning of $283.20 per ton from $290.50 on Friday.</p>
<p>Most of the sales were for prompt shipment because the price premiums offered for July soymeal discouraged buyer interest, dealers said.</p>
<p>Some soymeal basis offers for prompt shipment decreased because of last week's larger soybean crush and an increase in soybean sales to crushers since last week.  </p>
